## Why This Is Asked

Tests robustness of sorting mindset under memory constraints and heavy duplicates, plus guarantees on worst-case performance.

## Key Concepts

- Introsort: quicksort with a depth limit that falls back to heapsort
- Three-way partition: handles many duplicates efficiently
- In-place, cache-friendly data movement and tail recursion optimization

## Code Example

```javascript
function partitionDutch(a, lo, hi, pivot){
  let i = lo, lt = lo, gt = hi;
  while (i <= gt){
    if (a[i] < pivot){ [a[lt], a[i]] = [a[i], a[lt]]; lt++; i++; }
    else if (a[i] > pivot){ [a[i], a[gt]] = [a[gt], a[i]]; gt--; }
    else { i++; }
  }
  return [lt, gt];
}
```

